  "body": "What happens: The user picks an open run on the stock entity in 2D Contour. The route `contour_along_chain` walks the run's own points. It applies no radius offset. The tool centre rides the line. No test and no verifier check covers this route. The measurement of 2026-11-15 on main d1484f02a could not run it.\n\nExpected: One of these three results. The run is offset one tool radius to its air side, as the part-edge route does (`contour_run_side.rs` `contour_open_run`). Or the route is refused by name. Or a note on the page says that the tool centre follows the line.\n\nEvidence: Code reading of `contour_along_chain`. All routes that were measured put the centre 3.000 mm from the wall for tool D6. See #1777 for the older defect with the centre on the model edge.\n\nDone means: A test picks an open run on the stock entity. The test pins the chosen behaviour with a measured distance.\n\nRelated: #1927, #1929\n",
